{% doc %}
  Connection instructions: the house rules a client may show to the model. Sent by
  `initialize` (legacy) and `server/discover` (modern). The app authors its own through
  the instructions partial (Layer 2); the engine falls back to a short factual default
  when the app has none. The text is model-read, so it is security-relevant (§12.3):
  factual, short, no secrets, no threats and no claims about which text the model must
  trust. Clients list tools themselves, so it does not tell the model to call
  tools/list. It mentions documentation resources only when they are exposed. Clients
  may never fetch it, so anything an agent must obey also belongs in the tool
  descriptions.
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  function cfg = 'modules/mcp/helpers/config'

  assign instructions = null
  try
    function instructions = cfg.instructions_partial
  catch e
    assign instructions = null
  endtry
  if instructions == blank
    capture instructions
      echo 'This server gives access to a platformOS application. Every call acts as the '
      echo 'person who connected you and can do only what that person is allowed to do. '
      echo 'Pass arguments exactly as each tool input schema describes; arguments that do '
      echo 'not match are rejected, not guessed. A call refused as not permitted will be '
      echo 'refused again, so tell the user instead of retrying it; many refused calls in '
      echo 'a short time suspend the token this connection uses. Every call is recorded.'
      if cfg.resources.expose_markdown_pages == true
        echo ' Documentation pages are listed by resources/list.'
      endif
    endcapture
  endif
  assign instructions = instructions | strip
  return instructions
%}
